        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What documents do I need to import to Slovakia?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Required documents include commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, and EU GSP proof of origin. We also provide REACH compliance certificates.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can one order cover Slovakia alongside the Czech Republic?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We regularly prepare documentation for combined Slovak and Czech distribution from a single order, given how closely these two markets are usually managed together by the same buying teams.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How do you ensure fabric consistency across production runs?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Buyers sourcing workwear and uniform programmes alongside fashion lines often need documented proof of shade consistency for their own compliance audits. We retain the original approved lab dip, check each bulk run against it with a spectrophotometer rather than by eye, and flag anything past tolerance before it ships.</p>
